{title: 616 - Soldiers of Christ, Arise}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #616 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 616}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Soldiers of Christ, arise,
[D]And put [G/B]your armor [A/C#]on,
[D]Strong in [Bm]the [D]strength [Em]which [D]God supplies
[A/E]Through His [Em]eternal [A7]Son
[D]Strong in [A7]the [D]Lord [G]of [F7]hosts,
[Em]And in His [Bm]mighty [A7]power,
[Bm]Who in [G]the [F#m]strength [Em]of [A]Jesus [B7]trusts
[Em]Is more [F#m]than [A]con-queror.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Stand then in His great [G/D]might,
[D]With all [G/B]His strength [A]endued,
[D]But take, [Bm]to [D]arm [Em]you [D]for the [A/C#]fight,
[A/E]The panoply of [A7]God;
[D]That, having all [G]things [F7]done,
[Em]And all [Bm]your [Em]conflicts [F#m]passed,
[Bm]Ye may [G]o'ercome [Em]through [A]Christ [F#/A#]alone,
[Em]And stand [F#m]entire [A7]at [D]last.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]From strength to strength go [G/D]on,
[D]Wrestle [G/B]and fight [A]and pray,
[D]Tread all [Bm]the [D]powers of darkness [Bm]down
[A/E]And win [Em]the well-fought [A7]day.
[D]Still let [A7]the [D]Spirit [F7]cry
[Em]In all [Bm]His [Em]soldiers, [F#m]"Come!"
[Bm]Till Christ [G]the [F#m]Lord [Em]who [A]reigns [F#/A#]on [B7]high
[Em]Shall take [F#m]the [A]conquerors [D]home.
{end_of_verse}
